uplink-sunrise-disease-vial-name = Foodborne virus
uplink-sunrise-disease-vial-desc = Two doses of an engineered foodborne strain. Use the vial on food or an open drink: contamination takes 3 seconds. Only the consumer becomes infected; the disease does not spread by touch or droplets. A virology visor detects contaminated items, and exact analysis reveals signs of engineering. The vial can also seed a Petri dish, consuming it.
disease-syndicate-foodborne-name = engineered enterovirus
disease-syndicate-foodborne-description = An engineered foodborne strain causing gastrointestinal symptoms. Transmitted only by consuming contaminated food or drinks.
disease-hint-syndicate-foodborne = Repeated artificial insertions detected in the genome: the strain is adapted for foodborne infection and does not spread by touch or droplets. Deliberate culture contamination is likely; inspect the patient's food and drinks.
disease-contaminator-popup-empty = The vial has no contamination doses left.
disease-contaminator-popup-no-content = There is nothing left to contaminate: the food or drink is empty.
disease-contaminator-popup-done = You discreetly add the culture to { $target }.
disease-contaminator-examine-uses = Contamination doses remaining: [color=yellow]{ $uses }[/color].
